        <title>And You? </title>
        <author>
            <name>Ting Lu</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://tingyinglu.com/and-you.html"/>
        <id>https://tingyinglu.com/and-you.html</id>
        <media:content url="https://tingyinglu.com/media/posts/20/Jing-Luo_Ni-Ni_01_features_683x500_01.jpg" medium="image" />
            <category term="works"/>
            <category term="wood"/>

        <updated>2026-09-14T01:17:56+08:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://tingyinglu.com/media/posts/20/Jing-Luo_Ni-Ni_01_features_683x500_01.jpg" alt="" />
                    ｜And You? 你呢?｜ Using the “whale fall” as metaphor, the work reflects&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://tingyinglu.com/media/posts/20/Jing-Luo_Ni-Ni_01_features_683x500_01.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <p>｜And You? 你呢?｜</p>
<p>Using the “whale fall” as metaphor, the work reflects on the cycle of life and renewal. When a whale sinks into the deep, its body becomes nourishment for the ocean, sustaining ecosystems for decades. Death, then, is no longer an end, but a quiet act of exchange and giving. When our own lives come to stillness, can we too leave something that sustains others? Can the weight we carry in existence become a force of continuation beyond ourselves? And you? <span class="s1">Ｗ</span>hat do you want to leave to the world?</p>
<p class="p1">以「鯨落」為隱喻，探討生命的遞循與再生。「鯨落」<span class="s1">——</span>當巨鯨死後沈入海底，其軀體化為萬物的養分，能滋養整個生態系統數十年，延續生命於死亡之後。這是一場關於消逝與延續的對話，關於存在的重量與意義。死亡不再是終點，而是一場持續的交換與給予。當一切歸於靜止，我們能否仍為世界留下養分？你呢？你想能為世界留下什麼？</p>
<p>W17 x D9 x H25 cm<br>Lime wood, walnut, acrylic paint 椴木、胡桃木、壓克力顏料</p>
